@emersion, @Joshua-Ashton, it seems that the change to use wrap-git for `stb` (https://github.com/Plagman/gamescope/commit/2cea675db0157c1dc221c5b7fc574690c60d10e8) made the project very diffcult to build and package in sandboxed environments, including `flatpak-builder`.

The issue is that in such environments all the sources are cloned/downloaded in a preparation stage, usually as git modules, git submodules and tarballs, and then Internet access is no longer allowed for any of the following stages, including the build and install stages. In this case, however, the build stage is exactly when Meson attempts to clone the `stb` repository, and as far as I can tell there's no way around this without introducing downstream patches.

Also, why are we treating `stb` like a system library? It's not meant to be used this way. It doesn't have a buildsystem or a concept of "install", and doesn't offer a `.pc` file for discovery by buildsystems. It really should be a git submodule.

